        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Cleaning a humidifier is mostly about timing. Empty and refill it with fresh water every day, descale with vinegar and then disinfect separately once a week, and replace wicks and cartridges on schedule. That routine prevents nearly all the pink slime, mold, white dust and weak mist people blame on the machine.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When it is time to buy a new one, pick the design you will actually clean: a wide top-fill tank, a simple base and dishwasher-safe parts where offered. Our <a href="/best-humidifier/">best humidifier guide</a> ranks models with that in mind.
          </p>
